{
  "domain": "qa/stress_domains/nested_pieces",
  "note": "A null offered for a value-object argument that declares a command-level `default:` is not an absent argument. `fill_defaults` fills only a key the caller left out, so Ruby keeps the null, builds `CardNote` from its own fields (`text` has no default) and refuses TypeMismatch on `CardNote.text`, whether the card is addressed or not. Rust's generated `from_json` sent a null to the declared default (`text: none`), so it stored the default on a routed card and refused NotFound on an unaddressed one. `Board.Card.Remark`, two hops down, is the case the QA sweep SW-nested_pieces-1793458649 found.",
